# Native Platform Development Guidelines

## 🤖 Android Development

### Project Structure
```
android/
├── build.gradle              # Build configuration
├── src/main/
│   ├── AndroidManifest.xml   # Manifest file
│   └── java/com/adobe/marketing/mobile/reactnative/
│       └── {module}/         # Module implementation
```

### Build Configuration (`build.gradle`)
```gradle
android {
    compileSdkVersion 34
    buildToolsVersion "34.0.0"
    namespace "com.adobe.marketing.mobile.reactnative.{module}"
    
    defaultConfig {
        minSdkVersion 21
        targetSdkVersion 34
    }
}

dependencies {
    implementation "com.facebook.react:react-native:+"
    implementation "com.adobe.marketing.mobile:{aep-module}:+"
}
```

### Package Naming Convention
- **Namespace**: `com.adobe.marketing.mobile.reactnative.{module}`
- **Class naming**: `RCTAEP{ModuleName}`
- **Consistent with iOS**: Match bridge method names

### Java/Kotlin Patterns
```java
@ReactModule(name = RCTAEPModuleName.NAME)
public class RCTAEPModuleName extends ReactContextBaseJavaModule {
    public static final String NAME = "RCTAEPModuleName";
    
    @Override
    public String getName() {
        return NAME;
    }
    
    @ReactMethod
    public void methodName(String param, Promise promise) {
        try {
            // Call native AEP SDK
            ModuleName.method(param, new AdobeCallback<Type>() {
                @Override
                public void call(Type result) {
                    promise.resolve(convertToWritableMap(result));
                }
            });
        } catch (Exception e) {
            promise.reject("ERROR_CODE", e.getMessage(), e);
        }
    }
}
```

## 🍎 iOS Development

### Project Structure
```
ios/
├── RCT{ModuleName}.xcodeproj/    # Xcode project
├── src/
│   ├── RCT{ModuleName}.h         # Header file
│   ├── RCT{ModuleName}.m         # Implementation
│   └── RCT{ModuleName}DataBridge.h  # Data bridge (if needed)
└── RCT{ModuleName}.podspec       # CocoaPods specification
```

### CocoaPods Specification (`.podspec`)
```ruby
Pod::Spec.new do |s|
  s.name         = "RCTAEPModuleName"
  s.version      = "7.0.0"
  s.summary      = "Adobe Experience Platform ModuleName extension for React Native apps"
  s.homepage     = "https://github.com/adobe/aepsdk-react-native"
  s.license      = "Apache 2.0 License"
  s.author       = "Adobe Experience Platform SDK Team"
  s.platform     = :ios, "12.0"
  
  s.source       = { :git => "https://github.com/adobe/aepsdk-react-native.git", :tag => "#{s.version}" }
  s.source_files = "ios/src/**/*.{h,m,mm,swift}"
  s.requires_arc = true
  
  s.dependency "React-Core"
  s.dependency "AEPModuleName", "~> 5.0"
end
```

### Objective-C Patterns
```objc
// RCTAEPModuleName.h
#import <React/RCTBridgeModule.h>

@interface RCTAEPModuleName : NSObject <RCTBridgeModule>
@end

// RCTAEPModuleName.m
#import "RCTAEPModuleName.h"
#import <React/RCTLog.h>
@import AEPModuleName;

@implementation RCTAEPModuleName

RCT_EXPORT_MODULE(RCTAEPModuleName);

RCT_EXPORT_METHOD(methodName:(NSString *)param
                  resolver:(RCTPromiseResolveBlock)resolve
                  rejecter:(RCTPromiseRejectBlock)reject) {
    [AEPModuleName method:param completion:^(NSDictionary* result, NSError* error) {
        if (error) {
            reject(@"ERROR_CODE", [error localizedDescription], error);
        } else {
            resolve(result);
        }
    }];
}

@end
```

### Swift Integration
```swift
// For Swift files, use bridging headers
// RCTAEPModuleName-Bridging-Header.h
#import <React/RCTBridgeModule.h>
#import <React/RCTEventEmitter.h>

// RCTAEPModuleName.swift
@objc(RCTAEPModuleName)
class RCTAEPModuleName: NSObject {
    @objc
    static func requiresMainQueueSetup() -> Bool {
        return false
    }
    
    @objc
    func methodName(_ param: String, 
                   resolver resolve: @escaping RCTPromiseResolveBlock,
                   rejecter reject: @escaping RCTPromiseRejectBlock) {
        AEPModuleName.method(param: param) { result, error in
            if let error = error {
                reject("ERROR_CODE", error.localizedDescription, error)
            } else {
                resolve(result)
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## 🔧 Best Practices

### Error Handling
- **Consistent error codes** across platforms
- **Meaningful error messages** for debugging
- **Promise rejection** for async operations
- **Null safety** checks

### Data Conversion
- **iOS**: Use `NSDictionary` / `NSArray` for complex data
- **Android**: Use `WritableMap` / `WritableArray`
- **Maintain consistency** between platform implementations

### Performance
- **Background threads**: Don't block main thread
- **Memory management**: Proper cleanup of native objects
- **Callback handling**: Ensure callbacks are called once

### Testing
- **Unit tests** for native modules when possible
- **Integration tests** with sample app
- **Platform-specific testing** on real devices

